  "name": "STOOL EXAM FOR PH AND REDUCING SUBSTANCE",
  "code": "STPH",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>Test</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Normal Range / Expected Result</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Abnormal Findings</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Clinical Interpretation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Stool pH</strong></td>\n<td><strong>6.5 &ndash; 7.5 (neutral to slightly acidic)</strong></td>\n<td><strong>pH &lt; 5.5</strong></td>\n<td>Suggests carbohydrate malabsorption (e.g., lactose intolerance, other disaccharidase deficiencies).</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td><strong>pH &gt; 7.5 (alkaline stool)</strong></td>\n<td>May indicate bacterial overgrowth, protein malabsorption, or infection.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Reducing Substances (Benedict&rsquo;s test on stool)</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Negative</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Positive&nbsp;</strong></td>\n<td>Indicates presence of unabsorbed sugars&nbsp; suggests carbohydrate malabsorption (e.g., lactose intolerance, glucose-galactose malabsorption, other sugar intolerances).</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
